# The Vercel CLI uploads from the working directory, not from git, so
# .gitignore does not apply here. Without this, `vercel --prod` tries to
# upload the Flutter app's build output — a ~150MB debug APK plus Gradle and
# Dart caches — and fails on the 100MB per-file limit.
#
# Deliberately NOT excluding services/ or eval/: those are pnpm workspace
# members (see pnpm-workspace.yaml), and removing their package.json files
# would make the lockfile fail Vercel's frozen-lockfile install. apps/mobile
# is not a workspace member, so it can go entirely.

apps/mobile/

# Build output, regenerated on Vercel by vercel.json's buildCommand.
**/build/
**/dist/
**/.next/
**/out/
**/node_modules/
**/.dart_tool/
**/.gradle/

# Signing material must never leave this machine.
**/*.apk
**/*.aab
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
